SOAPBOX: The first night started with good conditions, and big EU stations showed up early. Then, after approximately 4:30 AM, suddenly no more EU signals came in and the expected EU sunrise peak simply didn’t happen. At least there was a small highlight with VK2GR and DU7ET.
SOAPBOX: The next night was horrible. I struggled to get heard even by US stations, and only a handful called in. After 04:30—ironically the exact time when EU conditions died on the first night—a few more EU stations made it through. But again, no real EU sunrise peak.
SOAPBOX: As many others have already said, these were the worst conditions ever.
SOAPBOX: In years like this, with such poor condx, locations like Aruba are not exactly favorable. But new year, new luck!
